      "side": 1,
      "message": "updateSuccessValue hardcodes the skip-count assuming a fixed 3-line auth stack (first module skip 2, second skip 1, implicit third \u003d deny). This is undocumented and fragile — if the stack has more/fewer modules (e.g. a platform adds another auth line), this silently produces wrong success\u003d counts without any validation. Worth a comment explaining the assumption, or deriving the count from the actual number of remaining lines rather than hardcoding.",
      "revId": "267e824dcabb3a26c7bb27b4d34b897ed2593634",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
